<h1>Basic Configuration Parameters group</h1>
<p>The <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/">Folder Parameter test</a> we just
  built doesn't stand on its own - it's one of several tests bundled together under a <strong>test group</strong>
  called <strong>Basic Configuration Parameters</strong>, each demonstrating a different configuration field type.
  You've already seen this group in the execution tree:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/folder-parameter-test-gui.png", "Basic Configuration Parameters test group expanded in the Orcraft controller's Test Explorer, showing all its parameter tests", "large") }}
<p>Let's review the code of the file that defines this group:</p>
{{ cmd.copyPath("orcraft-test-suite-tutorial/test_group_basic_configuration_parameters/") }}

<h2 id="group-file-structure">Group file structure</h2>

<h3 id="imports">Imports</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('from __future__ import annotations

from orcraft import (
	OrcraftTestGroup,
	OrcraftTestGroupConfig,
	OrcraftTestGroupResult,
	OrcraftConfigField,
)

from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_folder_parameter.test_folder_parameter import TestFolderParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_boolean_parameter.test_boolean_parameter import TestBooleanParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_selector_parameter.test_selector_parameter import TestSelectorParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_folder_list_parameter.test_folder_list_parameter import TestFolderListParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_file_parameter.test_file_parameter import TestFileParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_file_list_parameter.test_file_list_parameter import TestFileListParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_numeric_parameter.test_numeric_parameter import TestNumericParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_multi_selector_parameter.test_multi_selector_parameter import TestMultiSelectorParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_string_parameter.test_string_parameter import TestStringParameter') }}
<p>Unlike a test, a group imports <code>OrcraftTestGroup</code> and <code>OrcraftTestGroupConfig</code> instead of
  <code>OrcraftTest</code> and <code>OrcraftTestConfig</code> - plus one import per test it bundles together.</p>

<h3 id="config-class">Config class</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('class TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersConfig(OrcraftTestGroupConfig):
	name = OrcraftConfigField.Text(default="Basic Configuration Parameters")
	description = OrcraftConfigField.Text(
		default="Covers tests that demonstrate configuration parameters used with the maze app."
	)
	tests = OrcraftConfigField.Tests(
		default_factory=lambda: [
			TestFolderParameter(),
			TestBooleanParameter(),
			TestSelectorParameter(),
			TestFolderListParameter(),
			TestFileParameter(),
			TestFileListParameter(),
			TestNumericParameter(),
			TestMultiSelectorParameter(),
			TestStringParameter(),
		]
	)') }}
<p>Just like <code>name</code> and <code>description</code> on a test config, a group config has the same two
  fields - shown for the group itself in the execution tree. The field that matters here is <code>tests</code>,
  declared with <code>OrcraftConfigField.Tests</code>: it's a list of test instances, each one becoming a child
  node of this group in the execution tree, in the order given.</p>
<p>If you want to remove a test from showing up - and running - under this group, you can just comment out its
  line in this list, instead of deleting it.</p>

<h3 id="group-class">Group class</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('class TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersResult(OrcraftTestGroupResult):
	pass


class TestGroupBasicConfigurationParameters(OrcraftTestGroup):
	def __init__(self) -> None:
		super().__init__(config=TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersConfig())
		self.result = TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersResult()') }}
<p>Unlike a test, a group has no <code>_run_case</code> to implement - running it simply means running every test
  it contains. <code>TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersResult</code> is empty here, since this group doesn't
  add any result fields of its own beyond what <code>OrcraftTestGroupResult</code> already provides.</p>

<h3 id="main">Main</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('def main() -> None:
	group = TestGroupBasicConfigurationParameters()
	group.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
	main()') }}
<p>Running the group's <code>main</code> runs every test it contains, one after another, the same way the
  controller does when you run the group node itself.</p>

<h2 id="basic-configuration-parameters">Basic configuration parameters</h2>
<p>Here's a short summary of each test in this group and the parameter type it demonstrates. See the
  <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/">Framework</a> chapter for complete implementation details of each
  field type.</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Test</th>
      <th>Field type</th>
      <th>What it demonstrates</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/">Folder Parameter</a></td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Folder</code></td>
      <td>Runs the maze app executable with no arguments to display its help page.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Boolean Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Boolean</code></td>
      <td>Runs the maze app executable with or without the <code>--help</code> switch based on a toggle.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Selector Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Select</code></td>
      <td>Presents the available maze app commands as options and runs the selected one.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Folder List Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.FolderList</code></td>
      <td>Selects multiple folders and runs once per selected folder.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>File Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.File</code></td>
      <td>Uses a file path for save/load operations with the maze app.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>File List Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.FileList</code></td>
      <td>Selects multiple files, using each one for a save/load operation, running once per file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Numeric Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Numeric</code></td>
      <td>Configures maze dimensions, seed, and start/end coordinates.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Multi-Selector Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.MultiSelect</code></td>
      <td>Selects one or more solving algorithms and runs once per selection.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>String Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Text</code></td>
      <td>Optionally passes a raw command-line string to the maze app.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
